From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: Reused buffers for the SRTP copies and the fragments of a frame

sendMediaBatch allocated a protected copy of every packet and the H.264/H.265 packetizers a buffer for every
fragment, all freed after the frame. musl's allocator then created slot groups of the packet size class for
each frame and unmapped them afterwards, so each frame paid mmap, munmap and page faults. Both now reuse
their buffers from frame to frame: the protected copies live until the synchronous batch send returns (a copy
that is still held elsewhere is replaced), the fragments until they are packetized.
